{"ref":"BDB, קַדְמָה","hw":"קַדְמָה","html":"† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">קַדְמָה</span>]</big>  <strong>n.f. antiquity, former state</strong>;—<br><strong>1.</strong>  <em>antiquity, beginning</em>, sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">קַדְמָתָהּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 23:7\" href=\"/Isaiah.23.7\">Is 23:7</a> (of Tyre).<br><strong>2.</strong>  <em>former state</em>, sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">קַדְמָתָן</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:55\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.55\">Ez 16:55</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <span dir=\"rtl\">קַדְמַתְכֶן</span> v <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 16:55\" href=\"/Ezekiel.16.55\">55</a>; pl. sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">קַדְמוֹתֵיכֶם</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 36:11\" href=\"/Ezekiel.36.11\">36:11</a>.<br><strong>3.</strong>  cstr. sg. = <strong>conj.</strong> <em>before</em> (temp.; Aramaic) <span dir=\"rtl\">שֶׁקַּדְמַת שָׁלַף</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 129:6\" href=\"/Psalms.129.6\">ψ 129:6</a>.","next":"BDB, קִדְמָה","prev":"BDB, קֵ֫דֶם"}